type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

!! Overview

Adds four everyday fields to the tiddler edit template:

|!Field |!Control |!Stored value |
|`nature` |controlled vocabulary, single value |a bare slug (`concept`, `guide`, …) |
|`status` |controlled vocabulary, single value |a bare slug (`stable`, `raw`, …) |
|`project` |free text, with a dropdown of the values already used in the wiki |free text |
|`tools` |list field, edited like tags, on the Tags row |a list of titles |

`nature`, `status` and `project` share the ''Type'' row: the four controls sit on one flex line and shrink evenly — Type included — so the row always fits the tiddler width, wrapping instead of overflowing when the tiddler is narrow. `tools` shares the ''Tags'' row, as a second box of the same kind driven by the core `tag-picker` macro — the two pickers stay strictly independent: the tools dropdown offers the values already used in `tools`, never the wiki's tags, and vice versa.

!! Controlled vocabularies

Only the slug is ever written to the field. Icons and labels are display-only, resolved at render time, so a wiki stays readable and filterable in any language:

* the //allowed values and their order// live in the `list` field of `vocab/nature` and `vocab/status`
* the //icons// live in `vocab/icons.multids`, keyed `<field>/<value>`
* the //labels// live in `language/<lang>/vocab.multids`, keyed `Vocab/<field>/<value>`

Adding, removing or reordering a value is done in the plugin source, not through the UI — there is no vocabulary editor, on purpose: a value added through the interface could not carry its translations. To add one, append its slug to the relevant `list` field, then add its icon and its label in each language. A value with no label falls back to its own slug; a value with no icon simply renders without one.

Shipped out of the box:

* `nature` — concept, ref, guide, pattern, snippet, template, decision, log, hub, task, tasklist, routine
* `status` — archived, deprecated, stable, raw

Two helpers are exposed globally for use in view templates and lists: `<<bf-vocab-item field value>>` renders icon + label, and the `bf-vocab-label` / `bf-vocab-icon` / `bf-vocab-values` functions give the pieces separately.

!! How it works

Sharing a row means sharing a flex container, and the edit template renders each of its sections as a separate block — so the plugin ships a verbatim copy of two core tiddlers with the extra controls inserted inside them:

* `$:/core/ui/EditTemplate/type` — Nature, Status and Project go into the existing `tc-edit-type-selector-wrapper`
* `$:/core/ui/EditTemplate/tags` — the tags box and the tools box go into one flex row

Three consequences worth knowing:

# they are ''core overrides'' — upgrading TiddlyWiki will not bring in upstream changes to those two tiddlers until this plugin is updated too
# the stylesheet neutralises the core `min-width` computed by `set-type-selector-min-width`, which otherwise keeps the type control from shrinking
# the edit template defines the tag input's state tiddlers once for the whole form; the tools picker shadows them (`$:/temp/NewToolName…`), without which the two pickers would share one input and a half-typed tool name would be added as a //tag// by the save keyboard shortcut

!! Requirements

TiddlyWiki >= 5.3.0. No other dependency.

